# Fingerprints of findings that have been reviewed and confirmed NOT to be
# secrets. One per line, in the form:
#
#   <commit-sha>:<file-path>:<rule-id>:<start-line>
#
# Get the fingerprint from a verbose scan:
#   gitleaks git --staged -v
#
# Prefer this file over widening an allowlist in .gitleaks.toml: an entry here
# silences exactly one occurrence and shows up in `git blame`, whereas an
# allowlist silences a whole class of findings forever.
